      "content": "This perception stems more from the heterogeneous nature of the labor market, where formal industrial training levels can be highly inconsistent across different regions within Sub-Saharan Africa. While individual work ethic is strong, infrastructure variability and differing norms around hierarchical direction often necessitate more direct oversight initially. To justify management costs, frame this as an investment in establishing strong operational standardization rather than a reaction to inherent worker unreliability.",
